cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  fab-optimization: predictive lot dispatching for a 300mm
  semiconductor fab
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the
  metadata below. Please also cite the two works it depends on: the
  PySCFabSim baseline simulator and the SMT2020 testbed, both listed
  under references.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alton
    family-names: Alexander
    email: alton@frontanalytics.com
repository-code: https://github.com/altonalexander/fab-optimization
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-08-30
keywords:
  - semiconductor manufacturing
  - lot dispatching
  - scheduling
  - constraint programming
  - CP-SAT
  - discrete event simulation
abstract: >-
  A predictive lot dispatching system for a 300mm semiconductor fab.
  Tactical assignment is formulated as a CP-SAT model solved with
  Google OR-Tools; the contribution is the decomposition and the
  ranking reformulation -- priority ranking rather than scheduling,
  tool-group rather than per-tool granularity, and a four-hour
  horizon -- not the solver. Results are measured against a pinned
  PySCFabSim baseline reading the same SMT2020 load, so the
  dispatcher and the baseline are always compared on identical input.
references:
  - type: software
    title: OR-Tools
    authors:
      - given-names: Laurent
        family-names: Perron
      - given-names: Vincent
        family-names: Furnon
    url: https://developers.google.com/optimization/
    repository-code: https://github.com/google/or-tools
    version: 9.15.6755
    notes: >-
      Provides the CP-SAT solver used for the tactical layer. Pin the
      version when quoting any benchmark number -- solver performance
      changes between releases.
  - type: software
    title: PySCFabSim
    url: https://github.com/prosysscience/PySCFabSim-release
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      The baseline simulator, vendored and modified in
      baselines/pyscfabsim/. Every comparison number this project
      reports was produced by it.
  - type: article
    title: SMT2020 -- A Semiconductor Manufacturing Testbed
    authors:
      - given-names: Denny
        family-names: Kopp
      - given-names: Michael
        family-names: Hassoun
      - given-names: Adar
        family-names: Kalir
      - given-names: Lars
        family-names: "Mönch"
    journal: IEEE Transactions on Semiconductor Manufacturing
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1109/TSM.2020.3001933
    notes: >-
      The fab dataset both the dispatcher and the baseline read.
      Cite this for any published result derived from it.
